---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import register from "../data/register.json";
import { people } from "../lib/people.js";
import changes from "../data/changes.json";
import corrections from "../data/corrections.json";
---
<Base title="About"
      eyebrow="What this is, who it is for, and the rules it keeps"
      dek="An evidence-first archive of one family's maternal line — Arienzo in the province of Caserta, to Brisbane. Every claim carries its confidence or is marked unproven.">

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.2rem">
    <p><strong>This is the maternal line of one family, followed backwards from Brisbane to a single
    street in a small town in Campania.</strong> Nine generations, from a Matteo Falco born by about
    1735 on <strong>strada Camellara</strong> in Arienzo, to a generation living in Australia now.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:.6rem">It is built for <strong>one reader's descendants</strong>, and it is
    public because a family history that lives on one laptop dies with the laptop.</p>
  </div>

  <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(120px,1fr));gap:.6rem;margin:1rem 0">
    <div class="card" style="padding:10px 14px"><div class="mono" style="font-size:1.5rem">{register.length.toLocaleString()}</div><div class="small">records</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="padding:10px 14px"><div class="mono" style="font-size:1.5rem">{people.length}</div><div class="small">people identified</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="padding:10px 14px"><div class="mono" style="font-size:1.5rem">{corrections.length}</div><div class="small">published corrections</div></div>
    <div class="card" style="padding:10px 14px"><div class="mono" style="font-size:1.5rem">{changes.length}</div><div class="small">recorded changes</div></div>
  </div>

  <h2>The five rules</h2>
  <ol class="rules">
    <li><strong>Every claim carries its confidence, or is marked unproven.</strong> Documented,
    inferred, disputed, family lore — and <a href={u("/dna")}>dna</a>, which ranks below documented
    because a register entry names a person and an estimate names a probability.</li>

    <li><strong>Negatives and nulls are published.</strong> If a search was run and found nothing,
    that is written down, so nobody repeats it. <a href={u("/searched")}>What has been read →</a></li>

    <li><strong>Corrections are visible, never silent.</strong> A withdrawn reading stays on the page
    that carried it. Where the family tree still asserts something this archive discarded — Agostino
    Falcone at the head of the line — <strong>he is drawn struck through beside the man who replaced
    him.</strong> <a href={u("/corrections")}>Corrections →</a></li>

    <li><strong>A name is not a person, and a shared surname is not a relationship.</strong> This
    parish has three Maria Falco and four Pasquale; «Pasquale Falco» alone carries seventy-nine
    records. <strong>Nothing is merged on a name.</strong> <a href={u("/method")}>Method →</a></li>

    <li><strong>Living people are named, and nothing more.</strong> A name and a relationship — never
    a date, a place, a record or a photograph. That line was drawn on 10 September 2026, and
    <strong>the one time it slipped, the failure is on the corrections page.</strong></li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Where the evidence comes from</h2>
  <div class="scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Body</th><th>What it gives</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Antenati</strong> — the Italian state archives' portal</td>
        <td>The Arienzo civil death registers, <strong>read act by act rather than searched</strong>.
        Twenty-one volumes so far. <a href={u("/antenati")}>How →</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>FamilySearch</strong></td>
        <td>Handwriting-recognition full text over parish books nobody has indexed by hand, and the
        Benevento civil registration index.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Nudgee Cemetery, Brisbane</strong></td>
        <td>Fifteen burials, including generation seven and his wife in adjoining niches.
        <a href={u("/graves")}>Graves →</a></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>The family's own papers</strong></td>
        <td>An <em>estratto</em> from the Comune di Arpaia, a War Merit Cross citation, photographs,
        and a MyHeritage tree of 427 people — <strong>the last of which is unverified and labelled as
        such everywhere it appears.</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>

  <h2>How it is built</h2>
  <p>Static pages generated with Astro from plain JSON and TSV, all of it in
  <a href="https://github.com/daviddef/TheFalco" rel="noopener">the public repository ↗</a> — including
  the <a href={u("/research-log")}>working notes</a>, which keep the wrong readings alongside the
  corrections. <strong>Nothing on this site is asserted that cannot be traced back to a file you can
  open.</strong></p>

  <h2>What it is not</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Not a genealogy service.</strong> It follows one line and the town around it.</li>
    <li><strong>Not finished.</strong> <strong>258 volumes of <em>processetti</em> have never been
    opened</strong>, and the act that would settle generation seven's mother is in an unindexed
    Forchia register. <a href={u("/open-questions")}>Open questions →</a></li>
    <li><strong>Not neutral about its own mistakes.</strong> Twice in two days the same misreading was
    made, and saying so is treated as more useful than the finds.</li>
  </ul>

<style is:global>
  .rules{max-width:80ch}
  .rules li{margin:.7rem 0;line-height:1.6}
</style>
</Base>
